# Commit and PR Standards

## Commit scope
- Keep each commit to one logical unit of work.
- Avoid mixing refactor, feature, and formatting-only changes in one commit.

## Commit message quality
- Use imperative title (`fix`, `add`, `update`, `refactor`).
- Explain intent and impact, not only file changes.

## PR readiness checklist
- Include concise summary of behavior changes.
- Include test/analyze evidence relevant to touched scope.
- Call out risks, migration notes, and manual QA steps when needed.
